# Who reviews what.
#
# The point is not to block work — it is to make a change that crosses a boundary
# *visible*. Editing your own crate needs no ceremony; editing shared vocabulary or
# the app wiring should be seen by whoever depends on it.
#
# Replace the placeholders with real GitHub usernames before this does anything.

# Default: anything not matched below.
*                       @chillgamerboys

# The map. Terrain, tile spawning, and the settings that drive them.
/crates/hex_map/        @chillgamerboys
/assets/config/world.ron @chillgamerboys

# Gameplay: the player, movement, and whatever turn system arrives.
/crates/hex_units/   @chillgamerboys

# Shared vocabulary. A change here affects everyone by definition — HexCoord,
# HexSpan, the screen states, and the ordering sets all live here.
/crates/hex_core/       @chillgamerboys

# App wiring. The only crate that can see every other one.
/crates/hex_game/       @chillgamerboys

# Build, lint, and CI configuration. These are the guardrails themselves; a change
# that weakens one should be deliberate rather than incidental.
/Cargo.toml             @chillgamerboys
/clippy.toml            @chillgamerboys
/deny.toml              @chillgamerboys
/rust-toolchain.toml    @chillgamerboys
/.github/               @chillgamerboys
